  console.log("All attempts have been made, but the PIN was not found.");
  console.log("Attempts made:", attempts.length);
}

bruteforce(target, alphabet, attempts);
```

This code will attempt to find the target PIN by trying all possible 4-digit combinations using the provided alphabet. The attempted PINs are stored in the `attempts` array for reference. Keep in mind that this example is quite slow and inefficient, as it checks all possible combinations without any optimization. In a real-world scenario, you would want to optimize the bruteforcer to make it faster and more efficient.

Bruteforcing should be used with caution, as it can be time-consuming and may violate privacy or security policies. It's essential to use it responsibly and only for ethical purposes.

